# Code Standards

## General

- Match existing naming, package layout, and DI patterns in the touched module
- Minimize scope — only change what the task requires
- **Hilt always** — `@HiltAndroidApp`, `@HiltViewModel`, `@Module` in `di/`
- KSP for Room and Hilt compilers

## Comments

Default: **write no comments**. Only when WHY is non-obvious (hidden constraint, subtle invariant,
workaround). Never explain WHAT the code does. One short line max.

## ViewModel Pattern

- One ViewModel per screen
- `LiveData` / `Flow` via existing `arduia/mvvm-core` patterns (`EventLiveData`, `EventObserver`)
- ViewModels call repositories directly (no UseCase layer unless requested)
- `Result<T>` wrapper for async outcomes

## Fragment UI (current)

- View Binding in fragments
- Navigation via `main_nav.xml` + Safe Args
- Feature packages under `ui/<feature>/`

## Compose (v2 migration)

- New screens may use Compose when migrating
- Split route (with `hiltViewModel()`) from stateless content composable
- One `@Preview` per distinct UI state on content composables
- Match Material 3 patterns from existing theme

## Data Layer

- Room entities in `data/local/`; amounts stored as integer ×100
- Repository interfaces bound in `di/RepositoryModule.kt`
- Mappers implement `com.arduia.core.arch.Mapper<I,O>`

## Product Guards

- Max expense: 999,999,999.99
- No cloud backup features
- Privacy-first — no unnecessary network calls or data collection
